o chair angles while most are zero: build.py:51-55,74. Absolute scale and hidden layout cannot be inferred from a single view; no aligned world-space errors are asserted."],\n  "appearance_and_resource_analysis": ["The reference has faint wall hexagons, dark tables and warm wall light pools. The delivered image has a faint hexagonal pattern and light walls but appears flatter, with only one obvious lamp at the right and no similarly prominent paired wall-light pools. Reference image and executions/blender_1795841702424816251/artifacts/final.png; build.py:24-38,75-85.", "The floor material \'Pale stone floor\' is a uniform Principled material assigned to \'Floor\'; \'Warm ivory walls\', \'Charcoal grey tabletops\' and \'White molded chair plastic\' are similarly assigned. Source sets base color and roughness rather than constructing an image or noise mapping: final_source/build.py:6-10,19-22,45-48,65-69. Extracted detailed_state.json:81085-81355 records the floor material and its Principled BSDF output connection. The hex pattern is a separate beveled curve in world coordinates, not a mapped image: build.py:24-38. No image texture, coordinate mapping or packed texture is authored by the delivered source; original_inspection/capture/original/summary.json:3-7 reports no missing external images. No full-reference image plane is evidenced.", "Independent white-world images are evaluator products, not student tests; they retain camera, geometry and material confounds and do not establish a benefit: input_index.json:24-33; independent_evaluation/common_light/capture/common_light.png; reference_gt/common_light/capture/common_light.png."],\n  "geometry_analysis": ["Window panes are thin colored boxes mounted in front of a solid back wall rather than evidence of a cut opening; their material is named glass but the source creates an opaque default Principled shader: final_source/build.py:6-8,21,40-43. Chair backs are custom meshes with solidify and subdivision, seats and wheel